<ContentPage title="Karinderya Beginner Guide" seoTitle="Karinderya Beginner Guide | Karinderya Roblox Wiki" description="Learn the basics of serving customers, cooking orders, stocking ingredients, and progressing your Karinderya." kicker="Getting started" intro="A practical first-shift guide to the main restaurant systems." parent={{ label: 'Guides', href: '/guides/' }} relatedLinks={[{ label: 'Codes', href: '/codes/' }, { label: 'Food', href: '/food/' }, { label: 'Recipes', href: '/recipes/' }, { label: 'Workers', href: '/workers/' }, { label: 'Equipment', href: '/equipment/' }, { label: 'Grocery', href: '/grocery/' }, { label: 'Furniture', href: '/furniture/' }, { label: 'Decorations', href: '/decorations/' }]} sourceIds={['roblox-game', 'beginner-guide', 'codex-menu', 'wiki-furniture']} tableOfContents heroImage={siteImages.beginnerGuideHero}>
  <h2 id="learn-the-service-loop">Learn the service loop</h2>
  <ol><li>Seat or assign customers when the current interface allows it.</li><li>Read the customer order before committing ingredients.</li><li>Cook the order on an available stove.</li><li>Serve the completed order and continue the customer flow.</li></ol>
  <h2 id="keep-ingredients-available">Keep ingredients available</h2>
  <p>Use the <a href="/grocery/">Grocery</a> to replace ingredients your current menu needs. Check the current in-game listings when planning purchases because availability can change between updates.</p>
  <h2 id="upgrade-around-the-bottleneck">Upgrade around the bottleneck</h2>
  <p>Better stoves can reduce cooking time, while better furniture can improve the dining area. Multiple cooking stations may help process orders in parallel.</p>
  <h2 id="progress-through-documented-systems">Build on core systems</h2>
  <p>Customer service contributes to menu progression. Workers may change Manual Assign behavior, and current codes can provide Cash or items. Review the linked pages as your restaurant grows.</p>
</ContentPage>
